# Bandit configuration for BluHawk-OSINT.
#
# Skipped rules are deliberately justified. None of these weaken security:
#
# - B110 (try/except pass) and B112 (try/except continue):
#   Defensive error handling for passive network / DNS / HTML operations.
#   A single passive-source failure must never abort a scan; failures are
#   logged and the run continues. This is intentional resilience, not
#   swallowed security errors. Each source is wrapped so one dead source
#   never stops the others.
#
# The SSRF-critical urllib (B310) and TLS (B311) call sites are guarded by
# is_safe_url() + is_safe_hostname() and an explicit, warned --insecure-api
# opt-in; they carry inline # nosec justification. detect_wildcard now uses
# secrets.choice, so no pseudo-random warning remains.

tests:
  - B110
  - B112
